What is ported, and how closely
-------------------------------

These are ports, not reimplementations. Where a number or a formula appears
below, it is Bloub's, unchanged, and the test suite asserts it stays that way.

  src/faces/expressions.js
      The sixteen expression poses — head yaw/pitch/roll, eye separation, and
      per-eye width, height, tilt and lid — transcribed from
      bloub/src/bot/expressions.ts and bloub/src/bot/face.ts (EYE_W, EYE_H,
      EYE_SPLIT, REST_GAZE). Verified field by field in
      test/expressions.test.mjs.
      The seventeenth face, "round", is original to this project.

  src/lib/geometry.js
      eyeFrames() — the sphere tangent-frame projection that places the eyes,
      after bloub/src/bot/face.ts eyePoses().

  src/bodies/shapes.js
      profileFromPolygon, hullOfCircles, superellipseProfile,
      unionOfCirclesProfile, roundedPolygon, regularPolygonProfile and the
      Catmull-Rom path emitter, from bloub/src/bot/shape.ts; the eight
      silhouette definitions and normalisation from bloub/src/bot/skins.ts.
      Verified radius by radius in test/shapes.test.mjs.

  src/bodies/palette.js
      The twelve-colour customiser palette from bloub/src/bot/skins.ts. One
      change: the pale "Cream" (#f1efe9) is pure white here.

  src/bodies/shapes.js (silhouette posing)
      poseSil/blendSil/toPoints/silPath/polyPath and the egg profile, from
      bloub/src/bot/shape.ts and bloub/src/bot/profiles.ts.

  src/lib/math.js
      The easing set (easeOutCubic, easeInOutCubic, easeOutQuint) from
      bloub/src/bot/math.ts. The animation timings were fitted against these
      exact curves.

  src/anim/decor.js
      The whole decor layer from bloub/src/bot/decor.ts: the hue wheel, the
      orthographic arc renderer with its front/back depth split, the seeded
      ring, swoosh and comet-ribbon tables, the three thinking dots, the burst
      particles and the notification pip constants.

  src/anim/states.js
      The fourteen-animation catalogue from bloub/src/bot/states.ts, with the
      measured constants intact — the exclamation-mark bars and teardrop, the
      triangle's 0.213 orbit radius, and every timing in every state.
      Verified in test/anim.test.mjs. See docs/decisions/0005-animation-catalogue.md.

What is original to Mote
------------------------

  src/anim/player.js — how a state is blended into the creature's ordinary
  life — is original, as is the rest of the behaviour layer: the valence/arousal/dominance affect model, the two
  timescales of emotion and mood, temperament derived from the creature's
  name, the attention and oculomotor model (saccades, dwell, gaze breaks),
  the discrete-expression chooser with crossfade, the scripted episode player,
  and the maker/live application shell.

Bloub is itself a study of the x.ai bot avatar's visual behaviour. Neither
Bloub nor this project is affiliated with or endorsed by x.AI.

Blobatar
--------

The editable Sun body in src/bodies/shapes.js adapts Blobatar 2's radial-petal
silhouette concept. Mote expresses the petals as smooth lobes in its own 64-ray
profile and keeps its own eyes, expressions, fitting, renderer and animation.

